 "path": "continual_arc_full_lines_color_to_2.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC: recolor complete separator lines

Observed and verified on task `task-82643032` (2026-09-29): in an input dominated by a background color, identify rows and columns consisting entirely of a single separator color and recolor those entire lines to `2`; leave all other cells unchanged. The demo used separator color `3` and had complete border/separator bands (including adjacent full columns). The test used separator color `1`: full rows 6, 18, and 19 and full columns 5 and 17 were changed to `2`; all other cells were preserved. The submitted 20x18 output was confirmed CORRECT with zero wrong attempts.

For similar future instances, verify that candidate separator rows/columns are uniform and apply the color change only to entire such lines. Do not recolor isolated appearances of the separator color in nonuniform rows/columns."
